SUMMARY:🎃  Halloween Dinner @ The Haunted Keg Mansion 👻
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🎃 
 **Halloween Dinner @ The Haunted Keg Mansion 👻**\n\nThis year marks our
  **14th annual Halloween Dinner at The Keg Mansion** — a tradition I sta
 rted with this group fourteen years ago.\n\n⚠️ **This event fills up e
 very year\, and spots are limited to just 30 people. If you want to join u
 s\, please make sure you’re committed before signing up.**\n\nIf you don
 ’t already know\, The Keg Mansion is one of the most haunted buildings i
 n Toronto. Some guests claim to have seen the Lady in the window upstairs\
 , and the women’s washroom is famous for its ghostly encounters. We may 
 not know exactly where we’ll be seated\, but the second floor is known t
 o be especially active… if you dare. 👻\n\n📱 Don't forget to join o
 ur **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi0
 18gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🍽️ The Keg Mansion\n\nThe Keg is a classi
 c steakhouse with a wide range of dishes and price points\, so there’s s
 omething for everyone. Whether you’re coming for the meal\, the company\
 , or the possibility of encountering something from the other side\, you
 ’ll be part of one of our longest-running Halloween traditions.\n\n📋 
 **Menu:**[ Click Here](https://thekeg.com/en/locations/mansion/menu)\n💲
  **Cost of Meal:** $$$\n\n***\n\n## 👥 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup S
 pot:** I’ll be waiting outside The Keg Mansion wearing my Moose Hat. Ple
 ase don’t go inside without me.\n🕖 **Meetup Time:** 6:45 pm\n\n**I’
 ll only wait 5 minutes!**\n\n***\n\n## 🎭 Dress Code & Church Street\n\n
 Every year people ask if they can dress up — the answer is **YES!** Cost
 umes are welcome. 🎃\nAfter dinner\, anyone who wants to head to **Churc
 h Street for Toronto’s famous Halloween Festival** is welcome to go.\n\n
 It gets **very crowded**\, so I won’t be joining the group or leading ev
 eryone through the festival. I’ll help anyone who wants to go together f
 ind one another\, point you in the right direction\, and make sure you kno
 w where you’re headed.\nFrom there\, you’re on your own to enjoy the m
 adness! 👻\n\n***\n\n## 💵 SAVE YOUR SPOT — PLEASE READ BEFORE RSVPi
 ng\n\n**Spots are limited to 24 people.**\n\nTo secure your spot\, a **$25
  e-transfer must be sent to [mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmacle
 an@hotmail.com) within 24 hours of signing up.**\nThis applies to **everyo
 ne**.\n\nIt does not matter whether you joined the group yesterday\, have 
 been here for fourteen years\, or have been a member in good standing for 
 years. **If you are attending this event\, you pay the $25 save-your-spot 
 fee. There are no exceptions.**\n\nHere’s how it works:\n\n* **$25 must 
 be paid within 24 hours of signing up.**\n* **$20 will be returned to you 
 when you show up.**\n* **$5 is the Meetup fee that supports the group.**\n
 * If payment is not received within 24 hours\, **your spot may be given to
  someone else.**\n* **There are no refunds for any reason.**\n\nPlease do 
 not sign up unless you are **100% committed to attending**. With only 30 s
 pots available\, every spot matters.\nI’m not going to chase people for 
 payment. If you sign up\, you are responsible for sending the $25 within t
 he 24-hour deadline.\n\n⚠️ **Waiting List:** If the event is full and 
 you are placed on the waiting list\, **do not send the $25 e-transfer.** O
 nly send payment if I contact you and confirm that a spot has become avail
 able. Your spot is not confirmed until I have contacted you and confirmed 
 it.\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ Important Notes\n\n* Sometimes things happen and I
  may need to cancel — please watch for updates.\n* Please **don’t call
  the restaurant** — they won’t know anything about this event. Direct 
 all questions to me.\n* This group is open to everyone: singles\, couples\
 , and anyone looking to be social\, make friends\, and have fun. We also h
 ost movies\, walks\, hikes\, arts & culture outings\, and more!\n\n👤 **
 Organized by Mathew.** For questions\, post on the wall or email **[toront
 omoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)
 **
