SUMMARY:NEW TRAIL! 🍂 From Scarborough to North York: The Fall Colours T
 rail Walk 🌈
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🍂 
 From Scarborough to North York: The Fall Colours Trail Walk 🌈\n\n### A 
 Scenic Fall Adventure Through Trails\, Ravines & Toronto History\n\nToront
 o has some wonderful natural spaces tucked between its neighbourhoods\, an
 d this walk connects two of them into one longer adventure!\n\nWe’ll beg
 in in Scarborough\, exploring the **Gatineau Corridor Trail**\, with its w
 ildflowers\, tall grasses\, and green spaces where nature is allowed to gr
 ow a little more freely. 🍁 From there\, we’ll make our way along some
  city streets before connecting with another trail system and continuing t
 hrough the surrounding ravines toward the **Rainbow Tunnel**.\n\nThe tunne
 l is an unusual piece of Toronto history\, painted in 1971 by teenager B.C
 . Johnson as a tribute to his friend Sigred\, who died in a car accident. 
 Although the artwork has seen better days\, we’ll make a quick stop to s
 ee it before continuing toward our final destination.\n\nWe’ll finish at
  **Shops at Don Mills**\, where anyone who wants to can join us for coffee
 \, a pastry\, or something to eat after the walk. ☕🥐\nThis is a longe
 r outing than some of our regular walks\, but we’ll take our time\, enjo
 y the scenery\, and have a break along the way.\n\n***\n\n### 🚶‍♂
 ️ What We’ll Do\n\nAlong the route\, we’ll:\n\n* Explore the Gatinea
 u Corridor Trail and its naturalized green spaces 🌼\n* Walk through par
 ks and neighbourhood streets\n* Take a break midway through the walk\n* Co
 nnect with the Moccasin Trail and surrounding ravine paths 🌳\n* Stop br
 iefly at the Rainbow Tunnel 🌈\n* Continue to Shops at Don Mills\n* Fini
 sh with an optional coffee or snack with the group ☕\n\nThe walk should 
 take approximately **3 hours**\, depending on the pace of the group and th
 e conditions along the route.\n**Please note:** This is a point-to-point w
 alk. We will not return to our starting location at Dollar Tree. At the en
 d\, I’ll help anyone who needs assistance figuring out their transit opt
 ions.\n\n***\n\n### ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk takes place
  in typical Toronto weather conditions. Please dress appropriately for the
  forecast and wear comfortable walking shoes.\nThe route includes a mix of
  paved streets\, trails\, and potentially uneven or unpaved surfaces. Ther
 e will be some distance to cover\, so this walk is best suited to people w
 ho are comfortable walking for around three hours\, with breaks.\n\nThis i
 s a social walk\, not a race. We’ll keep a steady pace and make time to 
 enjoy the surroundings.\n\n🌦️ **This event happens rain or shine!**\n
 \n***\n\n### 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Starting Location:** Outside th
 e Dollar Tree near Kennedy Station\n🫎 **Look for me wearing my Moose Ha
 t!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM\nI will only wait 5 minutes.\n**Early 
 is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Shops at Don Mills\, N
 orth York\n🚇 **Transit:** We’ll finish near the Eglinton line. I’ll
  help anyone who needs directions for getting home by transit.\n\n***\n\n#
 ## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer to [mathewmacle
 an@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee helps suppor
 t the group and allows us to continue organizing walks and other events th
 roughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n### ☕ After the Walk\n\nOnce we reach Shops 
 at Don Mills\, anyone who wants to continue the outing can join us for cof
 fee\, pastries\, or a bite to eat.\nIt's a chance to relax\, chat\, and ge
 t to know one another after our walk. Participation is optional.\n\n***\n\
 n### 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n
 🥨 A snack\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n📱 Your phone or camera
  for photos\n\n***\n\n### 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:
 \n\n* People who enjoy discovering hidden parts of Toronto\n* Anyone inter
 ested in local history and unusual landmarks\n* Walkers who enjoy explorin
 g trails and ravines\n* People looking to meet others and make friends\n* 
 Anyone who wants to spend a few hours outdoors enjoying the fall colours\n
 \nThe trails and Rainbow Tunnel are part of the adventure\, but **the peop
 le you meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:
 ** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you'
 re unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may nee
 d to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for
  updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall
  or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesando
 utings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for the trails.**\n**Stay for the conversa
 tion.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂
 💛
